        <h2>8th Central Pay Commission: Strategic Framework & Key Projections</h2>
        <p>
          The constitution and implementation of the <strong>8th Central Pay Commission (8th CPC)</strong> represents an essential financial revision for more than 48 lakh Central Government employees and over 100 lakh state government staff across India. Anticipated implementation between 2026–2027, the 8th CPC will follow the landmark 7th Pay Commission recommendations introduced in 2016 and set new benchmarks for public sector compensation, pension structures, and cost-of-living indexation.
        </p>
