      <section class="content-block">
        <h2>Fitment Factor Analysis: How Basic Pay Revisions Are Formulated</h2>
        <p>
          The primary mathematical driver of basic pay and pension revisions in Indian Pay Commissions is the <strong>Fitment Factor</strong>. This uniform multiplier converts existing 7th CPC Basic Pay into 8th CPC Basic Pay across all levels and grades. A fitment factor of 2.28, for example, means that a current basic pay of ₹35,400 becomes ₹80,712 (35400 × 2.28).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="content-block">
        <h2>The 8th CPC Pay Matrix Architecture (Levels 1 to 18)</h2>
        <p>
          The Pay Matrix structure eliminates subjective grading by distributing central government designations into specific functional bands. Understanding your classification ensures accurate salary projections post-8th CPC implementation.
        </p>
      </section>

